.TH TIR 1 "2026" "tir v0.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tir \- kitchen timer with notification, speech, and countdown
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tir
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ wait ]
.RI [ what ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tir
is a command line kitchen timer for Apple macOS 10.9 (Mavericks) and later.
It will show the message on terminal, notification center, and read it out
using audible speech.
The default message is "Tea is ready" and the "tea" is replaced by the
command argument.
If the first argument is a number, the command waits that time in seconds.
.PP
Time can be specified with suffixes:
.BR 60 " (seconds),"
.BR 3min " (minutes),"
.BR 1h " (hours),"
or
.BR 5:30 " (minutes:seconds)."
.PP
Countdown messages are announced every 10 minutes (>10min),
every minute (>1min), then at 30, 20, 10, and 5 seconds.
Use the
.B \-c
option to set a fixed interval, or 0 to disable.
.PP
If Music is playing, its volume is faded to half by default during
a speech.
Select control from
.IR fade ", " volume ", " pause " or " no
by the
.B \-i
option.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-w " time"
Wait time (default: 0).
.TP
.BI \-m " message"
Set message format (default: "%s is ready").
.TP
.BI \-c " time"
Set countdown interval (default: adaptive, set 0 to disable).
.TP
.BI \-C " count"
Set message repeat count (default: 1).
.TP
.BI \-I " time"
Set message repeat interval in seconds (default: 2).
.TP
.BI \-v " voice"
Choose speech voice (default: Fred).
Use
.B \-v \&?
to list available voices.
.TP
.B \-r
Same as
.BR "\-v random" .
.TP
.BI \-l " voice"
Choose voice for last message.
.TP
.BI \-b " sound"
Choose notification sound (default: Default).
Use
.B \-b \&?
to list available sounds.
.TP
.BI \-V " volume"
Set system sound volume temporarily (0\-100).
Volume is restored after one second.
.TP
.BI \-i " control"
Music control during speech:
.IR fade " (default),"
.IR volume ", " pause " or " no .
.TP
.BI \-W " count"
Set syllable count manually for
.B \-G
option.
.TP
.BR \-e / \-E
Echo message or not (default: yes).
.TP
.BR \-n / \-N
Send notification or not (default: yes on macOS).
.TP
.BR \-s / \-S
Speak or not (default: yes on macOS).
.TP
.B \-R
Ramen shortcut (3 minutes).
.TP
.B \-Y
Yakisoba shortcut (4 minutes).
.TP
.B \-U
Udon shortcut (5 minutes).
.TP
.BR \-GR ", " \-GY ", " \-GU
Gorgeous versions of
.BR \-R ", " \-Y " and " \-U .
These use the "Good News" voice to sing the completion message to a melody.
The message format is automatically adjusted based on the syllable count
of the target word to match the melody timing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tir 60
Wait 60 seconds and say "Tea is ready".
.TP
.B tir 180 Ramen
Wait 180 seconds and say "Ramen is ready".
.TP
.B tir 5min Your noodle
Wait 5 minutes and say "Your noodle is ready".
.TP
.B tir \-c 10 10min
Wait 10 minutes with countdown every 10 seconds.
.TP
.B tir \-GR
Gorgeous ramen timer (3 minutes with Good News voice).
.SH TIPS
Apple removed the voice "Good News", used by the
.B \-G
option, from the default voice list on recent operating systems.
You can download it from System Preferences:
select Accessibility, then Speech, and choose Customize in the
System Voice pulldown.
.SH BUGS
When used with the
.B \-G
option, the command counts syllables using a very simple algorithm,
which sometimes produces incorrect results.
Use the
.B \-W
option to manually specify the correct syllable count.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR osascript (1),
.BR say (1)
.PP
